# FALLBACK reverse-proxy option for https://lumoraos.in - only use this if
# the WHM Include Editor / userdata vhost route (deploy/apache/lumoraos.in.conf)
# isn't available to you. Use ONE of the two, never both - they configure
# the same proxying two different ways and will fight each other.
#
# STATUS as of 2026-08-12: deployed and currently returns a 500 on this
# specific VPS. Confirmed (by fully removing these rules and re-testing)
# that the rules themselves are the cause, not something else on the site.
# This box turned out to be running LiteSpeed Web Server, not stock
# Apache (see deploy/apache/lumoraos.in.conf's header for how that was
# found) - LiteSpeed has its own proxy implementation, so "enable
# mod_proxy" may not be the right fix. Root/server-log access is needed
# to get the precise error and correct fix - don't assume the note below
# about EasyApache4 applies as-is until that's confirmed.
#
# mod_rewrite's [P] (proxy) flag needs mod_proxy + mod_proxy_http loaded
# server-wide on stock Apache (WHM > EasyApache 4, root-only - see
# deploy/README.md), but unlike ProxyPass, RewriteRule ... [P] is
# normally allowed from .htaccess under cPanel's default "AllowOverride
# FileInfo" for a domain's docroot, so deploying this file itself needs
# no root access - just copy/rsync it to /home/lumoosr/public_html/.htaccess.
#
# Deploy: append (don't overwrite - cPanel puts its own PHP-ini directives
# in this file) to /home/lumoosr/public_html/.htaccess. Back up first -
# see deploy/README.md, "Do not overwrite unrelated cPanel files".

RewriteEngine On

# /storage/uploads/* and /api/v1/* -> NestJS API container (127.0.0.1:3000).
# main.ts serves uploaded files from /storage/uploads and everything under
# API_PREFIX (/api/v1) - see apps/api/src/main.ts.
RewriteRule ^storage/uploads/(.*)$ http://127.0.0.1:3000/storage/uploads/$1 [P,L]
RewriteRule ^api/v1/(.*)$          http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1/$1 [P,L]
RewriteRule ^api/v1$               http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/v1 [P,L]

# Everything else (including the web app's own unversioned legacy routes -
# /api/health, /api/generate, /api/brand-brain/extract, /api/copilot,
# /api/agents/run - which never collide with /api/v1/*) -> web container
# (127.0.0.1:3100).
RewriteRule ^(.*)$ http://127.0.0.1:3100/$1 [P,L]

# ProxyPreserveHost is deliberately NOT set here - unlike ProxyPass,
# mod_proxy restricts it to "server config, virtual host" context only.
# Including it in .htaccess (even with full AllowOverride) doesn't just
# get ignored - it makes the ENTIRE .htaccess file fail to parse, which
# is why this returned a 500 for every request, including ones that don't
# match any of the rules above. Confirmed via cPanel's Errors page
# 2026-08-12: "ProxyPreserveHost not allowed here". Not needed anyway -
# nothing in this app derives behavior from the proxied Host header
# (FRONTEND_URL/APP_URL are explicit config, not read from incoming
# requests). If that ever changes, use the WHM vhost-include method
# instead (deploy/apache/lumoraos.in.conf), where this directive IS valid.
RequestHeader set X-Forwarded-Proto "https"
RequestHeader set X-Forwarded-Port "443"
